(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"7d3da8a1-c6db-0646-b116-d618b43d4f3d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"aee2ad21-504c-944b-b1c0-01bdafe4481a"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"321553fe-0fd3-1248-8969-408c8c1bc201"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"9ad1b700-4eb0-9b44-aee8-1b62048308d2"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5e28c4bd-eec3-664b-9464-d79f4e436279"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"60a93b2b-13a6-e14c-875a-d9dce790ba54"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8eddb86b-d0e6-a348-bdf0-8f52827ed27d"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9b248205-769a-de4b-b153-01a302d8dfde"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e4b615ba-3ff9-9648-8c0a-111e39d0ae01"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ede48db5-6b74-3a4e-b481-3ed27c93fbe1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f68c581-6487-f744-91e4-9755424b245a"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"01a380b9-b61d-5445-a401-76416ee36fa3"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a617fe71-b877-544d-87d0-ce912f18c6c2"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"275a3a34-b1d9-5f4f-ae9b-a3dbe9411268"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"7747993d-2dd0-d440-a6c4-c729dc281e71"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3fed45f2-eb41-0943-ad9c-711cc232cd5a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d10f6ce8-\
ef34-b449-aad1-c74418d7ebde"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"d80af053-eb1d-ff4a-8473-f931387a8a42"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b37127b4-b111-bc46-9868-7de8ee595442"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b59343db-\
b2e6-c24f-8dac-1db7e4b0bf09"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"2223645e-aaaf-794d-a405-b73cd633dc2e"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b284d29d-a41c-a043-8c3e-95a74516cd48"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d3698d8f-4dc2-8f42-aad2-b9ea54706b82"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"848db649-41f5-204b-8872-b8566b87d8dc"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"15b176e3-3acd-294e-a1f4-cdf61c8cb8d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"8e718ee0-\
0310-494e-9bee-c47cb143005d"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"687a93cc-4ee9-8847-8130-e15057d4f71b"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8c2c07e2-a0ee-0d4d-9215-2bcef2c5bf16"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"9e34615d-\
0e6b-0a48-8c4e-9f5f187bdb35"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"9a09d473-7cd3-c246-91fd-4c6f95ea2cce"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"731fb017-8e9d-2e4e-8038-2bb871ab261d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"587f4cf4-\
d08a-0f4b-8d2f-0e3740417c98"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"4f3d0f85-f6a7-8743-9b2b-19fd253a96cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a4dab9b8-17da-8d4d-979d-31a58aa5d27c"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"564441f8-64c0-3a48-a2ef-273c5b5b9a3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ae833814-6b8e-bf40-a017-98ac549e859a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"506a0761-a74b-8948-80b2-d1fb230ad453"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"24909cd6-e45e-8e46-ad85-881fb5a2db57"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "24f78305-c75e-a642-9ed7-309529560bf4"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"cdfa7f15-7bf3-ef44-b977-7b054bfa1d70"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
